TRISC enum match misalignment regression
========================================

Reproduces the `std r4, r3, r0` MisalignedAccess fault discovered by the
TRISC test runner (audit item #19) when matching on a parameterized
enum like `Result[T, E]` whose payload contains another enum.

    module sysl.tests.enum_misalign

    enum Inner
        A
        B(value: int)

    enum Outer
        First(inner: Inner)
        Second

    #test
    test_match_outer_first() -> unit
        val o: Outer = First(B(42))
        o match
            First(i) ->
                i match
                    A -> assert(false, "expected B")
                    B(v) -> assert(v == 42, "got value")
            Second -> assert(false, "expected First")
